<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yeshwantrao Ghorpade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1908–1996</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Murarirao Ghorpade</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yeshwantrao <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghorpade">Ghorpade</a> was the last ruling raja of the princely state of Sandur in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, succeeding in 1928. He introduced reforms including a representative assembly and public services, and acceded to India in 1947 before Sandur merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> Province in 1949. He later served as a minister in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yeshwantrao-ghorpade.jpg" alt="Yeshwantrao Ghorpade" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yashwantrao_Hindurao_Ghorpade.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
